    <bpmn:process id="W_W948" name="W948. Social Commerce Order Processing (Facebook, Instagram, TikTok Shop)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer places order or expresses purchase intent via social media channel (Facebook Marketplace, Instagram Shopping, TikTok Shop, Facebook page DM, or Instagram DM)
Frequency: ~8,000–12,000 orders/month (growing 15–20% quarterly)
Volume: 1–5 items per order; average order value PHP 2,200 (lower than web/app AOV)
Owner: Ecommerce Manager
Participants: Social Commerce Associate, Customer, Ecommerce Operations, Payment Gateway, Fulfillment Team, Category Manager
Source: workflow W948 — Social Commerce Order Processing (Facebook, Instagram, TikTok Shop)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W948_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W948_Lane1" name="Social Commerce Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W948_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W948_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W948_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W948_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W948_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W948_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W948_Lane3" name="Ecommerce Ops">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W948_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W948_Lane4" name="Ecommerce Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W948_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W948_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W948_Start6" name="Customer places order or expresses purchase intent via social media channel (Facebook…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W948_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W948_Task7" name="Channel Monitoring &amp; Inquiry Capture">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Channel Monitoring &amp; Inquiry Capture: Social Commerce Associate monitors all active channels: (a) Facebook page messages and Marketplace inquiries; (b) Instagram DMs and Shopping tags; (c) TikTok Shop orders and comments; (d) automated chatbot captures basic inquiries (product availability, price, store location) 24/7 and escalates complex inquiries to human associate during business hours; (e) system ingests platform order feeds via API integration (TikTok Shop API, Facebook Commerce API, Instagram Shopping API) for direct platform orders
Responsible (R): Social Commerce Associate / Chatbot
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W948_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W948_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W948_Task8" name="Inquiry-to-Order Conversion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Inquiry-to-Order Conversion: For DM-based inquiries: (a) Social Commerce Associate responds within SLA (30 min during business hours, 2 hours off-hours); (b) identifies product(s) requested — uses product search by name, SKU, photo matching, or description; (c) confirms availability at customer&#x27;s preferred store (real-time inventory per W533) or DC; (d) provides product details, pricing, and fulfillment options (BOPIS, home delivery); (e) for order confirmation: creates order link via BuildRight&#x27;s secure payment page and sends to customer via DM; customer clicks link, reviews order, and pays online; order flows into ERP
Responsible (R): Social Commerce Associate / System
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Manager
Duration: 5–15 min/inquiry</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W948_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W948_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W948_Task9" name="Direct Platform Order Processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Direct Platform Order Processing: For TikTok Shop and Facebook/Instagram Shopping direct orders: (a) platform API pushes order to ERP in near-real-time; (b) system validates: (i) product availability — if unavailable, auto-responds to customer with alternatives or refund initiation; (ii) price sync — verifies order price matches current BuildRight price; (iii) shipping address validity — Philippine address validation per W310 master; (c) system creates order in ERP with social channel tag (TikTok/Facebook/Instagram), platform order ID, and customer data; (d) if customer is existing loyalty member (matched by mobile number), system links order to loyalty account for points earning
Responsible (R): System / Ecommerce Ops
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Manager
Duration: 2–5 min (mostly automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W948_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W948_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W948_Task10" name="Fulfillment Routing &amp; Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Fulfillment Routing &amp; Execution: Order routed to fulfillment per W536: (a) BOPIS → nearest store picks and stages per W11; (b) home delivery → DC or ship-from-store per W19/W19B; platform-specific shipping labels generated (TikTok Shop, FB/IG require platform-specific tracking numbers); fulfillment team packs and ships; tracking number pushed back to platform via API; customer receives platform-native tracking notification
Responsible (R): System / Fulfillment Team
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Manager
Duration: Per W11, W19</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W948_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W948_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W948_Task11" name="Financial Reconciliation &amp; Settlement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Financial Reconciliation &amp; Settlement: (a) platform settlement: each platform has different settlement cycles — TikTok Shop (T+3 to T+7), Facebook/Instagram (varies by payment method); system reconciles platform settlement reports against ERP order records; discrepancies (returns, cancellations, platform fees, shipping subsidies) flagged for review; (b) platform fee tracking: commission rates vary (TikTok Shop 1–5%, Facebook/Instagram Marketplace 5% per item); system records platform fees per order for margin analysis; (c) monthly: Social Commerce Associate reconciles all platform settlements against bank deposits and ERP revenue records per W99
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Ops / Finance
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Manager / CFO
Duration: Monthly (ongoing daily reconciliation automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W948_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W948_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W948_Task12" name="Channel Performance Analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Channel Performance Analytics: Weekly: Ecommerce Manager reviews channel performance — (a) orders, revenue, AOV by platform; (b) conversion rate (inquiry → order); (c) customer acquisition cost by channel; (d) return rate by platform; (e) platform fee as % of revenue; (f) top-performing product categories by platform; (g) content performance — which posts, videos, and live sessions generate the most orders; insights feed back to Marketing (W676) for content strategy and Merchandising (W1) for assortment decisions
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Manager / Social Commerce Associate
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W948_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W948_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W948_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W948_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W948_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-271 (ensure controlled execution — Marketplace &amp; Social Commerce (PA-10.3).) | - operational: (W50) serves as single source of truth
Owner: Ecommerce Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W948_Assoc15" sourceRef="W948_Annotation14" targetRef="W948_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
