    <bpmn:process id="W_W1209" name="W1209. E-Commerce Mega-Sale Event Preparation &amp; Execution (Lazada/Shopee 9.9, 11.11, 12.12)" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Marketplace platform announces mega-sale campaign dates (9.9, 10.10, 11.11, 12.12, Payday Sale, Lazada Birthday Sale, Shopee Super Shopping Day); typically 4–6 weeks before event
Frequency: ~28 sale events per year (24 payday sales on the 15th and 30th + 4 major platform campaigns, per the Background); ~8–10 per year are full-mobilization major events (per the Time Estimate)
Volume: 3.5–10× normal daily order volume (payday events at the low end, platform mega-sales at the high end, on the ~1,430 orders/day baseline); projected ~7,000–14,000 orders on a major event day
Owner: Ecommerce Manager
Participants: Ecommerce Manager, Category Manager, Pricing Analyst, DC Fulfillment Supervisor, Logistics Dispatcher, Customer Service Rep, Finance Manager, Marketing Coordinator
Source: workflow W1209 — E-Commerce Mega-Sale Event Preparation &amp; Execution (Lazada/Shopee 9.9, 11.11, 12.12)</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1209_LaneSet8">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1209_Lane1" name="Ecommerce Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1209_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1209_Task17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1209_Task18</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1209_Start9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1209_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1209_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1209_Lane3" name="Supply Planning Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1209_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1209_Lane4" name="Ecommerce Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1209_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1209_Lane5" name="DC Fulfillment Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1209_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1209_Lane6" name="Customer Service Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1209_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1209_Lane7" name="All Participants">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1209_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1209_End19</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1209_Start9" name="Marketplace platform announces mega-sale campaign dates (9.9, 10.10, 11.11, 12.12, Payday…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1209_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1209_Task10" name="Event planning kickoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Event planning kickoff (4–6 weeks before): Ecommerce Manager receives platform campaign brief from Lazada/Shopee account manager: campaign dates, available marketing tools (flash sale slots, banner placements, brand rewards), platform co-funding opportunities, commission rates, logistics support (free shipping vouchers); Ecommerce Manager convenes cross-functional preparation team
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1209_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1209_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1209_Task11" name="Product selection &amp; pricing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Product selection &amp; pricing: Category Manager selects participating SKUs (typically 500–1,000 items per event): (a) identify items with platform co-funding subsidies, (b) select clearance/seasonal items for flash sale, (c) bundle best-sellers for mega-deal packages, (d) Pricing Analyst calculates margin-acceptable promotional prices considering: platform commission (2–5%), co-funding offset, VAT impact, and target margin floor; (e) verify pricing consistency with own-site and in-store promotions per W523
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1209_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1209_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1209_Task12" name="Inventory pre-positioning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Inventory pre-positioning: Supply Planning Analyst reviews projected mega-sale demand per SKU: (a) estimate event-day demand (5–10× daily average for participating SKUs), (b) verify available stock at DC fulfilling ecommerce orders, (c) initiate emergency replenishment or transfer orders for at-risk SKUs, (d) for top 50 event SKUs: pre-pick and stage in ecommerce fulfillment zone at DC to accelerate Day-of processing
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Analyst / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 1 week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1209_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1209_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1209_Task13" name="System &amp; content preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: System &amp; content preparation: Ecommerce team: (a) uploads promotional pricing to marketplace seller center portals, (b) creates campaign-specific product listings with enhanced images and descriptions, (c) configures flash sale time slots, (d) sets stock caps per promo tier to prevent overselling, (e) tests voucher codes and promotional mechanics in staging environment, (f) updates own-site banners and landing pages for cross-channel consistency
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Coordinator
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Manager
Duration: 3–5 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1209_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1209_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1209_Task14" name="Fulfillment capacity planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Fulfillment capacity planning: DC Fulfillment Supervisor plans Day-of staffing: (a) schedule additional pickers and packers (seasonal temps or cross-deployed from DC operations), (b) pre-print shipping labels for top 100 predicted SKUs, (c) coordinate with 3PL partners for additional delivery vehicle availability, (d) set up overflow packing stations, (e) brief team on event-day priority and escalation procedures
Responsible (R): DC Fulfillment Supervisor
Accountable (A): DC Manager
Duration: 2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1209_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1209_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1209_Task15" name="Customer service readiness">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Customer service readiness: Customer Service Manager briefs CS team: (a) prepare FAQ templates for mega-sale-specific inquiries (shipping delays, stock availability, voucher usage), (b) pre-configure auto-reply rules for common queries, (c) schedule additional CS reps for event day and 3 days post-event, (d) prepare return/exchange surge capacity per W12A/W12B
Responsible (R): Customer Service Manager
Accountable (A): CX Manager
Duration: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1209_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1209_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1209_Task16" name="Event Day execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Event Day execution: System monitors real-time order flow: (a) Ecommerce Manager monitors seller center dashboards for order volume, stock levels, and flash sale sell-through rates, (b) DC Fulfillment Supervisor monitors pick-pack-ship queue against SLA targets (target: all orders shipped within 24 hours), (c) Logistics Dispatcher manages delivery dispatch for completed orders, (d) Category Manager monitors margin real-time — triggers stock cap reduction if margin floor breached by higher-than-expected volume, (e) Customer Service handles real-time inquiries
Responsible (R): All Participants
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Manager
Duration: Full day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1209_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1209_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1209_Task17" name="Post-event reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-event reconciliation (within 48 hours): (a) Ecommerce Manager compiles event performance: total GMV, order count, ASP, sell-through rate by SKU, new customer acquisition, platform commission cost, co-funding received, net margin; (b) DC Supervisor reports fulfillment metrics: orders shipped on-time, packing errors, stockout rate; (c) Finance Manager reconciles platform settlement vs. orders (Lazada/Shopee settle T+7 to T+14); (d) Customer Service reports return rate and top complaint categories
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Manager / Finance Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 4–6 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1209_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1209_Flow30</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1209_Task18" name="Post-event lessons learned">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Post-event lessons learned (within 1 week): Ecommerce Manager conducts retrospective: (a) what sold well vs. forecast, (b) fulfillment bottlenecks, (c) pricing effectiveness, (d) platform tool utilization, (e) customer feedback themes; documents action items for next mega-sale event
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Manager
Accountable (A): CMO
Duration: 2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1209_Flow30</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1209_Flow31</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1209_End19" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1209_Flow31</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1209_Annotation20">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-271 (ensure controlled execution — Marketplace &amp; Social Commerce (PA-10.3).) | - operational: Ecommerce Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Ecommerce Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1209_Assoc21" sourceRef="W1209_Annotation20" targetRef="W1209_Start9" associationDirection="None" />
