    <bpmn:process id="W_W5550" name="W5550. Marketplace Account Suspension, Enforcement Freeze &amp; Appeal Recovery Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: A marketplace platform (Shopee/Lazada/TikTok Shop) issues an account-level enforcement action against BuildRight&#x27;s seller account: seller-metric failure or penalty-point breach, listing-violation strike, IP/counterfeit complaint takedown, fraud-suspicion payout freeze, or full selling-privilege suspension/account deactivation
Frequency: Full or partial suspensions: rare, ~1–2 events/year across all platforms; lower-tier enforcement (mass listing takedowns, campaign exclusion, settlement holds): ~10–20 events/year
Volume: 1 event × the affected platform&#x27;s share of ~12,800 marketplace orders/month (≈30% of ~42,900 ecommerce orders/month per W1470) — a full Shopee-class suspension removes ~40–50% of marketplace demand overnight; settlement freezes hold PHP 15–40M of platform receivables
Owner: Ecommerce Manager / GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Participants: Ecommerce Associate, Content Manager, Category Manager (IP authorization letters), Finance Controller (settlement recovery), Customer Service Representative (order comms), VP Legal (IP/policy appeals), VP Marketing, IT (channel integration flags)
Source: workflow W5550 — Marketplace Account Suspension, Enforcement Freeze &amp; Appeal Recovery Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5550_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5550_Lane1" name="Ecommerce Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5550_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5550_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5550_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5550_Lane2" name="Ecommerce Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5550_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5550_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5550_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5550_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5550_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5550_Lane3" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5550_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5550_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5550_Start5" name="A marketplace platform (Shopee/Lazada/TikTok Shop) issues an account-level enforcement…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5550_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5550_Task6" name="Detection &amp; classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Detection &amp; classification: Seller Center / Seller Console notice, account-health dashboard alert, or platform partner-manager call; classify severity: (a) listing-level takedown (SKU strikes), (b) feature suspension (campaign exclusion), (c) settlement/payout freeze, (d) selling-privilege suspension, (e) account deactivation; capture the cited policy clause, evidence links, and the appeal window (typically 3–14 days); open the event record
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Associate / Ecommerce Manager
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: &lt; 4 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5550_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5550_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5550_Task7" name="Freeze-scope containment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Freeze-scope containment: pause marketplace ad spend; stop new listing pushes (W1464) and scheduled campaign participation (W1209); decide the order-acceptance posture (auto-pause storefront vs. honor in-flight orders); flag the channel integration so inventory allocation stops honoring the suspended storefront (W2412)
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Manager / IT
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: &lt; 8 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5550_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5550_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5550_Task8" name="Demand &amp; inventory re-routing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Demand &amp; inventory re-routing: redirect demand to the own webstore/app (W569-class own-channel listing) for marketplace-fulfillable SKUs; release stranded allocation; customer comms for in-flight orders, cancellation handling per W98 where needed
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Manager / Supply Planning
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5550_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5550_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5550_Task9" name="Evidence assembly &amp; appeal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Evidence assembly &amp; appeal: build the appeal pack — order logs and fulfillment proof (POD, chat records), brand-authorization letters from the Category Manager for IP complaints, the corrective-action statement citing the W1470 metric-remediation plan; file within the platform deadline; engage the platform partner manager at severity (c)+; track appeal status daily
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Manager / VP Legal / Category Manager
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 1–3 days (+ appeal window)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5550_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5550_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5550_Task10" name="Settlement-freeze accounting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Settlement-freeze accounting: recognize frozen platform receivables; reconcile platform settlement statements against ERP records per the W2414-class settlement chain; dispute improperly deducted penalties; re-forecast cash timing with Treasury when a freeze exceeds 30 days
Responsible (R): Finance Controller / Ecommerce Associate
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5550_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5550_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5550_Task11" name="Root-cause remediation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Root-cause remediation: fix the underlying defect before re-enablement — seller-metric corrective plan (W1470), listing/catalog corrections (W1464/W2408), the IP-takedown chain for counterfeit complaints (W3268), or the account-takeover chain where the enforcement stems from a compromised seller account (W3871)
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Manager / Content Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 1–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5550_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5550_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5550_Task12" name="Reinstatement &amp; verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Reinstatement &amp; verification: selling privileges restored (appeal won, penalty points expired, or suspension lifted); verify listing integrity, search placement, order flow and settlement resumption; re-enable ad spend only after seller metrics re-cross thresholds; confirm in the event record
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Associate / Ecommerce Manager
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 1–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5550_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5550_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5550_Task13" name="Post-event register &amp; prevention">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-event register &amp; prevention: log the event (platform, clause, appeal outcome, financial impact, days-down) in the channel-risk register feeding the platform-dependency review; add the violated policy clause to the listing-governance checklist (W1464) and the quarterly platform-rule watch (W1470)
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Manager
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 4 h</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5550_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5550_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5550_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5550_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5550_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-271 (ensure controlled execution — Marketplace &amp; Social Commerce (PA-10.3).) | - CTL-200 (ensure marketplace order &amp; settlement reconciliation.) | - operational: no appeal is filed without the corrective-action statement attached; ad spend is not re-enabled until seller metrics re-cross platform thresholds
Owner: Ecommerce Manager / GM, Digital Commerce Inc.</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5550_Assoc16" sourceRef="W5550_Annotation15" targetRef="W5550_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
